  "display_name": "fp8 scaled grouped gemm",
  "description": "Prepared indptr grouped GEMM, exact upstream API. Stored payload/scales and native caller output are unchanged. General source-derived inputs; no serving deployment or measured traffic.\n\nParameter domain: metadata.shape_domain defines dynamic request ranges and correlated model/ABI constraints; shapes.json fixes 10 representative workloads, not the complete support domain. Dispatched physical rows sum to M<=65536; each group has 0..8192 rows, aligned to 4. Logical rows cannot exceed physical capacity. For the FlashInfer segmented paths, logical_group_sizes is descriptive: all physical rows are computed; it does not imply masked execution. No measured traffic weights are claimed. Existing GPU evidence covers only the unchanged fixed sample, not every point in this dynamic domain.\n\nInput construction: Retain workload-v3 full projection/expert N/K geometry, legitimate small-M decode, long normal prefill, original physical group capacities, logical row counts, masking, alias and stress branches. FC2 activations for N/K=(4096,12288),(7168,2048),(4096,1536) are generated as SiLU(gate)*up with gate/up correlation .25, producing asymmetric heavy-tailed inputs. Projection/FC1 activations use Gaussian innovations with channel gains .65..1.35; weights use fan-in scaling, channel gains .65..1.35 and row gains .7..1.3. Existing channel-outlier controls remain. All profiles are quantized by the existing actual payload/scale encoder, so cross-group dynamic range reaches the operator. Before-quantization mean/RMS/absmax/third moment summaries describe up to 262144 sampled elements; correctness reads only stored payload/scale. The model configuration sources also define the MoE FC1 [2I,H]/FC2 [H,I] widths; selected TP shards are explicitly distinct from full-I configurations. Constant weights stay unchanged within an evaluation; no cold-cache or end-to-end layer-performance claim is made.",
